        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Joseph Smith\n- Organizations: Hudson's Bay Company (HBC)\n- Places: York Factory, Saskatchewan country\n- Topics: fur-trading posts\n\nFacts:\n- York Factory was built in 1684 as one of the first fur-trading posts established by the Hudson's Bay Company.\n- York Factory was used in the fur trade for more than 270 years.\n- Joseph Smith died in June 1765 while traveling from the Saskatchewan country to York Factory.",
